    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b378674cc21692aff6b898d3b3d39d3c3ff505f7ce12f1de608f87a8d2ae1192",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The frozen Hardy span uses Fourier inversion to turn Xi into moments governing derivatives of a theta kernel and shows how an eventual Xi sign would be amplified into derivative monotonicity. The Jensen construction instead expresses central completed-zeta coefficients as positive theta-tail moments and converts finite coefficient windows into polynomials whose fixed-degree asymptotics approach Hermite hyperbolicity.",
