      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Connes's quotient analysis turns orthogonality to periodizations into distributional support at zeros of an L-factor, whereas the difference-operator proposal formally constructs Hurwitz-zeta states and imposes boundary evaluation to select zeta zeros. Their comparison makes domain naturality, inverse choice, adjointness, and completeness the decisive tests of a spectral zero model.",
