    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d182773ff00398b4b198b0840d1081909fe1ae8f01398c44a3533d297416b399",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The parents actually describe three distinct mechanisms: first-pair dominance for one RH-conditional smoothed error, finite-block simultaneous phase recurrence for a different normalized prime-counting error, and many-frequency Gaussian reconstruction of local prime-power peaks. They do not support the proposed two-regime unification as written.",
