    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ec5e68c7124bb477fd2adf44afd7542ebf9cb0217b01589f92369b7ff8c1b703",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After unfolding removes mean zero density, random-matrix spectra model local fluctuation statistics, but characteristic-polynomial moments lack the Euler-product arithmetic factor. Independently, mesoscopic covariance is evaluated from a prime sum whose completion becomes log ζ near its pole, so the pole fixes the covariance scale in the stated off-critical regime.",
